tools.description:
Run a JavaScript program that calls MCP tools, and get back only what it returns. Use it in place of direct MCP tool calls: intermediate data stays out of the context.

The program is the body of an async function. Available:
- await call("mcp__<server>__<tool>", args) -> the tool result (parsed JSON when the tool returns JSON, else text)
- await recall(n) -> result #n of an earlier run, with no new call
- await sleep(ms) -> waits, to poll a slow job; the time limit of the run still applies
- await saveFile(name, data) -> writes data to a file and returns its path: text as it is, CSV or JSON lines for an array with a .csv or .jsonl name, else JSON; use it for data too large to return
- await readFile(path) -> the text of a file from saveFile
- console.log(...) -> shown after the result
- return <value> -> the result, as JSON

A result with images, audio or binary resources is { value, attachments }: each attachment has a file path, not the data. Return an image attachment to see the image.

A failed call throws an Error (catch it to continue). Promise.all runs calls in parallel, 8 at a time. There is no require, fetch, process or setTimeout: only these functions.

Write each tool name as a string in call("…"): a name built at run time is refused unless the config allows it.

Find tools and their argument types with search_tools first.

Examples:
// several reads, slimmed
const issues = await Promise.all(["A-1", "A-2"].map(key => call("mcp__tracker__get_issue", { key })))
return issues.map(i => ({ key: i.key, status: i.status }))
// a write and its check
await call("mcp__tracker__add_comment", { key: "A-1", body: "Fixed" })
return (await call("mcp__tracker__list_comments", { key: "A-1" })).some(c => c.body === "Fixed")
// a part of a large result
const log = await call("mcp__ci__get_log", { run: 42 })
return log.split("\n").filter(l => /error/i.test(l))

